{
  "body": "Add the gated canonical TCP provider and `latent:network/streams@0.1.0` host bridge. Connect, read, write, readiness, shutdown, close and affine chunks use the existing broker, I/O runtime, provider pools and original activation ledger. Endpoint policy stays distinct from typed HTTP authority. Original charges survive cancellation and rotation until actual resource destruction; node shutdown joins the bounded maintenance owner.\n\nInstallation requires the explicit development features. Ordinary nodes reject stream configuration, and this slice rejects host TLS. ADR-0061 and the qualification document retain the architecture/security, TLS, ordinary language, protected operator and measured-resource gates. Related implementation requirements remain open in #738, #739 and #740.\n\nRetained native/component evidence covers provider ownership, canonical calls, bounded DNS, HTTP-only denial, signed admission, cancellation, revocation, rotation and clean shutdown; each receipt keeps its original source identity. Current Linux validation also passes 28 source/inventory controls, three source-capacity controls, 71 Java SDK tests, complete CI command coverage and the actual pinned Java reference/ownership/model controls. Restore the qualifier's matching Java source closure without changing its assertions or limits. Fresh functional CI is required for this source integration; no production or whole-ticket qualification is claimed.\n",
